**Summary of behavior implemented:**

- `-H` / `--with-filename`: forces filename prefix on every selected line (one file, multiple files, or stdin as `(standard input)`).
- `-h` / `--no-filename`: suppresses all filename prefixes (one file, multiple files, stdin).
- Last occurrence wins regardless of spelling (short, clustered, long). E.g. `-h -H` → with; `-H -h` → without.
- Repetition of the same flag is idempotent (last one just re-sets the same mode).
- Default (neither flag): prefix for 2+ file operands, no prefix for one file or stdin.
- No panics on arbitrary bytes in paths or data; only `std` used; `unsafe` absent; `search_stream` remains the core line-selection entry point.
